## SECTION 3 — TOASTING MODULE

### 3.1 Performance Benchmark

The Revolution R180 Connect Plus defines the 2026 state of art in smart toaster hardware and establishes the minimum acceptable performance floor for ToastFlow AI. The R180 features InstaGLO 2.0 heating reaching full temperature in 2 seconds, 38 bread type profiles, 7 browning levels, real-time temperature sensor adjustment, and a 7-inch color LCD. ToastFlow AI must match or exceed these parameters to be defensible at a higher price point.

### 3.2 Heating System

Technology: Dual-zone hybrid — quartz infrared emitters (Zone A, outer) + nichrome resistance wire (Zone B, inner). This combination is superior to either alone: quartz provides the rapid surface sear that locks in moisture; nichrome provides sustained deep-heat penetration for thick artisan breads.

Rated power: 1,500W total
Mains input: 120V AC / 60Hz (US), 220V AC / 50Hz (EU — separate certified variant)
Peak current draw: 12.5A (US) / 6.8A (EU)
Heat-up time: ≤2 seconds to operating temperature (matching InstaGLO 2.0 benchmark)
Heating element isolation: Both zones on dedicated relay circuit, galvanically isolated from all logic power rails. Dual thermal fuses (one per zone, 280°C trip rating) as primary safety backstop.

### 3.3 Slot Specification

Slot width (adjustable): 32–42mm via spring-loaded auto-centering guide rails. This accommodates standard sliced bread (12mm) through artisan thick-cut (38mm) and brioche (34mm).
Slot length: 165mm — fits standard sliced bread and sub-sandwich slices
Number of slots: 2, independently controlled (each slot has its own heating zone relay and sensor set)
Guide rail material: Food-safe stainless steel 304, smooth interior to prevent bread tearing

### 3.4 Browning Control System

Levels: 9 discrete browning levels (vs. R180's 7 — finer granularity, differentiates medium-light from medium with optical precision)

Optical sensor array: 3× TCS34725 RGB color sensors mounted symmetrically along each slot (left edge, center, right edge). These sample bread surface color at 2Hz during the toasting cycle. Output: L*a*b* color coordinates used to compute browning index. Target browning uniformity: ΔE ≤ 3.0 edge-to-edge (colorimetric standard — perceptually indistinguishable by human eye below ΔE 3.0).

Temperature monitoring: 3× DS18B20 digital temperature probes (left slot wall, right slot wall, crumb zone). Resolution: 0.0625°C. Sampling: 1Hz. These feed the browning predictor model and detect thermal anomalies.

Bread type detection: 40+ modes. Classification is automatic via the on-device CNN (see Section 6) using optical sensor readings at initial bread insertion plus load cell weight reading. Includes: white, whole grain, sourdough, rye, gluten-free, frozen waffle, frozen bread, brioche, baguette slice, naan, crumpet, bagel (regular and large deli), English muffin, toaster pastry, and 25 further user-definable custom types.

Cycle performance:
Full toast time: 60–120 seconds depending on bread type and browning level
Repeatability: ≤5% cycle-to-cycle deviation on identical bread
Edge-to-edge uniformity: ΔE ≤ 3.0 (target), ΔE ≤ 5.0 (minimum pass criterion)

### 3.5 Lift Mechanism

Technology: Motorized auto-lift driven by 5V DC micro-gear motor via lead screw
Operation: Soft-landing on insertion (motor resists gravity), soft-lift on completion (motor-driven ascent at 15mm/s, no spring launch)
Post-lift position: Bread raised 45mm above slot top edge and held at fixed elevation — this is the spreading position used by the carriage system (see Section 4)
Emergency manual release: Push-button mechanical override bypasses motor for safety
Crumb tray: Full-width slide-out stainless steel pan, 2mm gauge, dishwasher-safe. MCU-tracked usage counter triggers on-screen "Clean Tray" reminder at configurable intervals (default: every 30 cycles).

