The ESP32-S3 is the confirmed optimal MCU for this application across all evaluated criteria.

Core specs as deployed in ToastFlow AI:
- CPU: Dual-core Xtensa LX7, 240MHz
- SRAM: 512KB internal + 8MB external PSRAM
- Flash: 16MB SPI NOR Flash
- AI acceleration: Vector SIMD instruction extensions for CNN/LSTM inference (TFLite Micro runtime)
- Wi-Fi: 802.11 b/g/n (Wi-Fi 4), 2.4GHz
- Bluetooth: BLE 5.0 (LE + Mesh)
- USB: USB OTG (firmware update via USB-C port on rear of appliance)
- GPIO: 45 programmable pins, sufficient for all peripherals listed below

### 5.2 Peripheral ICs and Sensors

Motor control:
- 2× DRV8825 stepper motor driver (carriage traverse motor + carousel not needed — carousel uses servo): SPI control, 1/32 microstepping capable, 2.5A max per phase, thermal shutdown protection
- 1× L298N dual H-bridge: lift motor (DC gear motor, 5V) and capsule clamping arm actuator

Sensing:
- 3× TCS34725 RGB color sensor: optical browning array, I2C bus, 16-bit resolution per channel, 700ms integration time
- 3× DS18B20 digital temperature probe: 1-Wire bus, -10°C to +125°C range, 0.0625°C resolution, 12-bit mode
- 1× HX711 24-bit ADC with load cell: bread presence detection, weight-based spread quantity verification (actual dispensed mass = post-dispense weight − pre-dispense weight of bread+tray), tare on empty tray at startup
- 1× ACS712-05B hall-effect current sensor on each motor supply rail: detects motor stall conditions (clog signal for auger — now retired — repurposed for carriage stall detection indicating capsule engagement failure)
- 1× RC522 RFID reader module (13.56MHz): mounted on carriage, reads capsule RFID tag at engagement
- 1× secondary RC522 fixed in carousel bay: reads all 4 capsule slots at load time to build a capsule inventory map

Display and UI:
- 4.3-inch IPS TFT LCD, 800×480 resolution, 400 nits brightness, capacitive 5-point multi-touch overlay
- Interface: SPI at 40MHz to ESP32-S3
- Brightness: auto-adjusting via ambient light sensor (VEML7700, I2C)
- UI interaction modes: touch, mobile app (BLE primary, Wi-Fi secondary), optional voice (app-mediated, cloud ASR)

Connectivity:
- Wi-Fi used for: cloud LLM API calls, OTA firmware updates, weather display (ambient feature), NTP time sync
- BLE used for: primary mobile app control (lower latency than Wi-Fi for real-time commands), direct device pairing without router dependency

### 5.3 Power Supply Architecture

Input: 120V AC / 60Hz (US primary), 220V AC / 50Hz (EU variant — separate certified transformer stage)

SMPS output rails:
- 5V / 3A: MCU, sensors, display, servo, RFID readers
- 12V / 2A: Stepper motor drivers, PTC heater relay, lift motor
- 3.3V / 500mA: ESP32-S3 core, RF frontend (LDO regulator from 5V rail)

Heating element circuit: Dedicated isolated 120V relay circuit. Relay rated 20A for safe margin over 12.5A peak load. No shared ground with logic circuits. Physical isolation gap ≥ 3mm on PCB (safety requirement for mains-adjacent traces).

Standby power consumption: <2W (meets EU Ecodesign standby requirement)
Operating efficiency: SMPS η ≥ 87% at full load

Safety:
- Dual thermal fuses on heating element circuit (280°C trip)
- GFI-compatible design (GFCI receptacle compatible, no grounding issue)
- Watchdog timer on ESP32-S3 (60-second software watchdog, hardware reset on timeout)
- All mains traces: ≥2.5mm clearance and creepage per IPC-2221 / UL requirements

